/* ==========================================================================
   Discord Audio Pipe — dark theme
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Palette (hex is repeated inline; Qt Style Sheets have no variables)

     titlebar chrome   #131417
     window / panel    #24262C
     control "well"    #1B1D21   (inputs sit below the panel, not above it)
     control hover     #212429
     control pressed   #17191C
     popup surface     #202329
     hairline border   #383C44   hover #4E545F
     focus ring        #6B76F0
     primary text      #E8EAED   muted #9AA0A6   titlebar #A8ADB5
     accent (mute)     #5561E8   hover #5C68EE   pressed #4550D4
     add / success     #43B581
     danger (close)    #D83C3E
     status healthy    #43B581   degrading #E9A23C   failing #F87171
     status idle       #9AA0A6
     on-air fill       #2E7D5B   hover #35845F   pressed #286B4E
     muted fill        #E9A23C   hover #F0AE50   pressed #D08F2E

   Contrast (WCAG 2.1, computed):
     #E8EAED on #24262C panel ....... 12.6:1
     #E8EAED on #1B1D21 control ..... 14.0:1
     #9AA0A6 muted labels on panel ... 5.7:1
     #A8ADB5 on #131417 titlebar ..... 8.2:1
     white on #5561E8 accent ......... 4.9:1  (hover 4.5:1)
     white on #D83C3E close hover .... 4.5:1
     #43B581 add glyph on control .... 5.7:1
     #6B76F0 focus ring vs control ... 4.4:1  (non-text, needs 3:1)
     arrow #6B6D72 vs control ........ 3.3:1  (non-text, needs 3:1)

   Status strip, all on the #1B1D21 well:
     #43B581 healthy ................. 6.6:1
     #E9A23C degrading ............... 7.8:1
     #F87171 failing ................. 6.1:1
     #9AA0A6 idle / metric text ...... 6.4:1

   Connect / Disconnect button, added with the connection state machine.
   Text ratios first (all clear 4.5:1), then the non-text rings and borders
   (which need 3:1, measured against BOTH neighbouring surfaces):
     #E8EAED idle label on #1B1D21 ... 14.0:1
     #43B581 idle hover on #212429 .... 6.1:1
     #38976C idle pressed on #17191C .. 4.9:1
     #E9A23C connecting on #1B1D21 .... 7.8:1   (also disconnecting)
     white on #2E7D5B live fill ....... 5.0:1
     white on #35845F live hover ...... 4.6:1
     white on #286B4E live pressed .... 6.4:1
     #A6C4B5 on #26493C live disabled . 5.3:1   (disabled text is exempt)
     #F87171 failed on #1B1D21 ........ 6.1:1
     #FCA5A5 failed hover on #212429 .. 8.2:1
     #D85C5C failed pressed on #17191C  4.7:1
     #A9B0F7 focus ring vs well ....... 8.2:1   vs panel 7.4:1
     #FFFFFF live focus ring vs fill .. 5.0:1   vs panel 15.1:1
     #43B581 live border vs panel ..... 5.9:1
     #E9A23C busy border vs panel ..... 7.0:1
     #F87171 failed border vs panel ... 5.5:1

   Mute button, checked (= muted):
     #131417 on #E9A23C amber fill .... 8.5:1
     #131417 on #F0AE50 hover ......... 9.5:1
     #131417 on #D08F2E pressed ....... 6.7:1
     #131417 focus ring vs the fill ... 9.5:1
     #E0D3B8 on #6B5528 disabled ...... 4.8:1   (should be unreachable)

   Muted is amber, not red: it is a state the user chose and will undo. Red
   is reserved for the two things that are actually wrong — a failed connect
   and a failing stream.

   The strip's failing colour is #F87171, not the #D83C3E used for the close
   button: #D83C3E is only 3.7:1 as text on #1B1D21, which is fine for a
   button fill behind white text but not for coloured text. Status is always
   spelled out in words as well, so colour is never the only channel.

   Qt Style Sheets support no transitions, shadows, transforms or variables —
   depth is done with flat layered surfaces and hairline borders only.

   Type
   ----
   assets/ ships Roboto Regular (400), Medium (500) and Black (900), all
   registered under the single family "Roboto", so weight is selected here
   with font-weight alone.

   Body text is 400. Emphasis is 500 and nothing else — the identity line,
   the column headers, the mute button and the status word. Black is
   bundled so the family has a full range, but the sheet does not reach for
   it: at 10–12pt on a dark ground a 900 weight blooms and, more to the
   point, when everything shouts nothing is emphasised. Medium is the whole
   distance needed to lift a label off body text at these sizes.

   Weight is stated explicitly on the base rule rather than left to
   default. If a face fails to register, Qt snaps the request to the
   nearest weight the family does have, so an unstated 400 is not a
   guarantee of 400 — it is a guarantee of "whatever loaded".
   ========================================================================== */


/* --- base ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

QWidget {
    background-color: #24262C;
    color: #E8EAED;
    font-family: "Roboto";
    font-size: 12pt;
    font-weight: 400;
}

QMainWindow {
    background-color: #24262C;
}

/* the "Logged in as: ..." status line; the labelled column headers below
   override this via the more specific QLabel#label rule */
QLabel {
    background-color: transparent;
    color: #E8EAED;
    font-size: 11pt;
    padding: 2px 2px 8px 2px;
}

/* the identity line is the one piece of state the window asserts about
   itself, so it carries the only emphasis in the header area */
QLabel#info {
    font-weight: 500;
}

QLabel#label {
    background-color: transparent;
    font-size: 10pt;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #9AA0A6;
    padding: 6px 2px 2px 3px;
}

QLabel:disabled {
    color: #63686F;
}


/* --- title bar ----------------------------------------------------------- */

QFrame#titlebar {
    background-color: #131417;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #0E0F12;
}

QFrame#titlebar QLabel {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    font-size: 10pt;
    color: #A8ADB5;
    padding: 7px 12px;
}

QFrame#titlebar QPushButton {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 0px;
    font-size: 11pt;
    color: #A8ADB5;
    min-height: 32px;
    min-width: 44px;
    padding: 0px;
}

QFrame#titlebar QPushButton:hover {
    background-color: #23252B;
    color: #E8EAED;
}

QFrame#titlebar QPushButton:pressed {
    background-color: #1A1C21;
}

QFrame#titlebar QPushButton:focus {
    background-color: #23252B;
    color: #E8EAED;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #6B76F0;
}

QFrame#titlebar QPushButton:disabled {
    color: #55595F;
    background-color: transparent;
}

/* these must out-specify "QFrame#titlebar QPushButton:hover" above, hence the
   redundant-looking descendant prefix */
QFrame#titlebar QPushButton#close:hover {
    background-color: #D83C3E;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QFrame#titlebar QPushButton#close:pressed {
    background-color: #B02F31;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QFrame#titlebar QPushButton#close:focus {
    background-color: #23252B;
    color: #E8EAED;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #D83C3E;
}

QFrame#titlebar QPushButton#minimize:hover {
    background-color: #23252B;
    color: #E8EAED;
}

QFrame#titlebar QPushButton#minimize:pressed {
    background-color: #1A1C21;
}


/* --- dropdowns ----------------------------------------------------------- */

QComboBox {
    background-color: #1B1D21;
    border: 1px solid #383C44;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #E8EAED;
    font-size: 11pt;
    min-height: 34px;
    padding-left: 12px;
    padding-right: 4px;
    outline: none;
}

QComboBox:hover {
    background-color: #212429;
    border-color: #4E545F;
}

QComboBox:focus {
    background-color: #212429;
    border-color: #6B76F0;
}

/* popup is open */
QComboBox:on {
    background-color: #212429;
    border-color: #6B76F0;
}

QComboBox:pressed {
    background-color: #17191C;
    border-color: #6B76F0;
}

QComboBox:disabled {
    background-color: #1A1B1E;
    border-color: #2A2D33;
    color: #5A5F66;
}

QComboBox::drop-down {
    subcontrol-origin: padding;
    subcontrol-position: center right;
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    width: 32px;
}

QComboBox::down-arrow {
    image: url(./assets/arrow-drop-down-line.svg);
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
}

/* the arrow SVG has a baked-in fill, so the disabled state keeps the same
   glyph and relies on the dimmed field around it */


/* --- dropdown popup list ------------------------------------------------- */

/* The popup is a QFrame container (QComboBoxPrivateContainer) wrapping the
   view. Left unstyled it paints the window colour, which shows as a dark
   square ring around the rounded list. Painting it the popup colour hides the
   corner slivers without relying on window translucency, which is not
   dependable across platforms. */
QComboBox QFrame {
    background-color: #202329;
    border: none;
}

QAbstractItemView {
    background-color: #202329;
    border: 1px solid #383C44;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #E8EAED;
    font-size: 11pt;
    padding: 4px;
    outline: none;
    selection-background-color: #2F3442;
    selection-color: #FFFFFF;
}

QAbstractItemView::item {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: #E8EAED;
    min-height: 32px;
    padding-left: 8px;
    padding-right: 8px;
}

QAbstractItemView::item:hover {
    background-color: #2A2E36;
}

QAbstractItemView::item:selected {
    background-color: #2F3442;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QAbstractItemView::item:disabled {
    color: #5A5F66;
}


/* --- popup scrollbar ----------------------------------------------------- */

QScrollBar:vertical {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    width: 10px;
    margin: 4px 2px 4px 0px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical {
    background-color: #3C414A;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 4px;
    min-height: 28px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical:hover {
    background-color: #4E545F;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical:pressed {
    background-color: #6B76F0;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:vertical,
QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    height: 0px;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:vertical,
QScrollBar::sub-page:vertical {
    background-color: transparent;
}

QScrollBar:horizontal {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    height: 10px;
    margin: 0px 4px 2px 4px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal {
    background-color: #3C414A;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 4px;
    min-width: 28px;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal:hover {
    background-color: #4E545F;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal:pressed {
    background-color: #6B76F0;
}

QScrollBar::add-line:horizontal,
QScrollBar::sub-line:horizontal {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    width: 0px;
}

QScrollBar::add-page:horizontal,
QScrollBar::sub-page:horizontal {
    background-color: transparent;
}


/* --- connect / disconnect button ----------------------------------------- */

/* One button per connection row, not two. The LABEL is the next action
   ("Connect" / "Disconnect" / "Retry"); the COLOUR below is the current
   state, published by gui.py as the dynamic property link="..." whose values
   are the constants in connection_state.py. Qt does not re-evaluate an
   attribute selector when a property changes, so gui.py does the
   unpolish/polish pair after setting it.

   The four looks are distinguishable without reading the word:
     idle           grey outline
     connecting     amber outline, dimmed (the button is disabled)
     live           SOLID GREEN -- the row is on air
     disconnecting  amber outline, dimmed
     failed         red outline

   Green-on-"Disconnect" is deliberate: the fill states what the row IS, the
   word states what the click DOES. */

QPushButton#connect {
    background-color: #1B1D21;
    border: 1px solid #383C44;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #E8EAED;
    font-size: 11pt;
    font-weight: 500;
    min-height: 34px;
    min-width: 108px;
    max-width: 108px;
    padding: 0px;
    outline: none;
}

/* -- idle: the offered action is "Connect" -- */

QPushButton#connect[link="idle"] {
    background-color: #1B1D21;
    border-color: #383C44;
    color: #E8EAED;
}

QPushButton#connect[link="idle"]:hover {
    background-color: #212429;
    border-color: #43B581;
    color: #43B581;
}

QPushButton#connect[link="idle"]:pressed {
    background-color: #17191C;
    border-color: #38976C;
    color: #38976C;
}

/* disabled here means "the selection is not complete yet"; the tooltip says
   which of device / server / channel is still missing */
QPushButton#connect[link="idle"]:disabled {
    background-color: #1A1B1E;
    border-color: #2A2D33;
    color: #5A5F66;
}

/* -- in flight: always disabled, never cancellable -- */

QPushButton#connect[link="connecting"],
QPushButton#connect[link="connecting"]:disabled,
QPushButton#connect[link="disconnecting"],
QPushButton#connect[link="disconnecting"]:disabled {
    background-color: #1B1D21;
    border-color: #E9A23C;
    color: #E9A23C;
}

/* -- live: on air -- */

QPushButton#connect[link="live"] {
    background-color: #2E7D5B;
    border-color: #43B581;
    color: #FFFFFF;
}

QPushButton#connect[link="live"]:hover {
    background-color: #35845F;
    border-color: #5FC79A;
}

QPushButton#connect[link="live"]:pressed {
    background-color: #286B4E;
    border-color: #38976C;
}

QPushButton#connect[link="live"]:disabled {
    background-color: #26493C;
    border-color: #2E5A49;
    color: #A6C4B5;
}

/* -- failed: the offered action is "Retry" -- */

QPushButton#connect[link="failed"] {
    background-color: #1B1D21;
    border-color: #F87171;
    color: #F87171;
}

QPushButton#connect[link="failed"]:hover {
    background-color: #212429;
    border-color: #FCA5A5;
    color: #FCA5A5;
}

QPushButton#connect[link="failed"]:pressed {
    background-color: #17191C;
    border-color: #D85C5C;
    color: #D85C5C;
}

QPushButton#connect[link="failed"]:disabled {
    background-color: #1A1B1E;
    border-color: #2A2D33;
    color: #5A5F66;
}

/* Last, so they win the specificity tie against the [link="..."] rules above
   and re-colour the ring without touching the fill. Two rules because a
   lavender ring on the solid-green live fill is only 2.4:1 against it, and a
   focus indicator has to be visible against BOTH the thing it surrounds and
   the panel outside it. White clears 3:1 on both (5.0:1 vs the green fill,
   15.1:1 vs the panel); lavender clears both on the dark outline states
   (8.2:1 vs the control well, 7.4:1 vs the panel). */
QPushButton#connect:focus {
    border-color: #A9B0F7;
}

QPushButton#connect[link="live"]:focus {
    border-color: #FFFFFF;
}


/* --- mute button --------------------------------------------------------- */

QPushButton#mute {
    background-color: #5561E8;
    border: 1px solid #5561E8;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    font-size: 11pt;
    font-weight: 500;
    min-height: 34px;
    min-width: 88px;
    max-width: 88px;
    padding: 0px;
    outline: none;
}

QPushButton#mute:hover {
    background-color: #5C68EE;
    border-color: #6B76F0;
}

QPushButton#mute:pressed {
    background-color: #4550D4;
    border-color: #4550D4;
}

QPushButton#mute:focus {
    background-color: #5C68EE;
    border-color: #A9B0F7;
}

QPushButton#mute:disabled {
    background-color: #333A5C;
    border-color: #333A5C;
    color: #8A90A8;
}

/* The button is checkable, so muted is a latched colour and not only a word
   swap. It keeps the word too -- "Resume" -- because colour is never allowed
   to be the only channel, but an amber button reads across several rows at a
   glance in a way that reading five labels does not.

   Amber rather than red: muted is a state the user chose and will undo, not
   a fault. Red is reserved for the failure states.

   These come after the plain rules above: an id + pseudo-state selector ties
   with another id + pseudo-state selector on specificity, so source order is
   what decides, and :checked:hover has to be spelled out for the same
   reason. */

QPushButton#mute:checked {
    background-color: #E9A23C;
    border-color: #E9A23C;
    color: #131417;
}

QPushButton#mute:checked:hover {
    background-color: #F0AE50;
    border-color: #F0AE50;
    color: #131417;
}

QPushButton#mute:checked:pressed {
    background-color: #D08F2E;
    border-color: #D08F2E;
    color: #131417;
}

/* Dark ring, not the lavender used elsewhere: on an amber fill the light
   ring vanishes (1.8:1) while #131417 reads at 9.5:1 against it. */
QPushButton#mute:checked:focus {
    background-color: #F0AE50;
    border-color: #131417;
    color: #131417;
}

/* Should not be reachable -- gui.py clears the mute whenever the row leaves
   LIVE, and the button is only enabled in LIVE -- but a latched control that
   greys out without un-latching would be asserting a mute that is not in
   effect, so it is defined rather than left to the plain :disabled rule. */
QPushButton#mute:checked:disabled {
    background-color: #6B5528;
    border-color: #6B5528;
    color: #E0D3B8;
}


/* --- add-connection button ----------------------------------------------- */

QPushButton#connection_btn {
    background-color: #1B1D21;
    border: 1px solid #383C44;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #43B581;
    font-size: 15pt;
    min-height: 34px;
    max-height: 34px;
    min-width: 34px;
    max-width: 34px;
    padding: 0px;
    outline: none;
}

QPushButton#connection_btn:hover {
    background-color: #212429;
    border-color: #43B581;
    color: #4FC48D;
}

QPushButton#connection_btn:pressed {
    background-color: #17191C;
    border-color: #38976C;
    color: #38976C;
}

QPushButton#connection_btn:focus {
    background-color: #212429;
    border-color: #6B76F0;
}

QPushButton#connection_btn:disabled {
    background-color: #1A1B1E;
    border-color: #2A2D33;
    color: #3B584B;
}


/* --- generic push buttons (fallback for anything unnamed) ---------------- */

QPushButton {
    background-color: #1B1D21;
    border: 1px solid #383C44;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #E8EAED;
    font-size: 11pt;
    min-height: 34px;
    padding: 0px 16px;
    outline: none;
}

QPushButton:hover {
    background-color: #212429;
    border-color: #4E545F;
}

QPushButton:pressed {
    background-color: #17191C;
}

QPushButton:focus {
    border-color: #6B76F0;
}

QPushButton:disabled {
    background-color: #1A1B1E;
    border-color: #2A2D33;
    color: #5A5F66;
}


/* --- loading spinner inside the mute button ------------------------------ */

QSvgWidget {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    max-width: 18px;
    max-height: 18px;
}


/* --- live status strip --------------------------------------------------- */

/* Sits in the same "well" surface as the inputs so it reads as instrument
   panel rather than as another control. */
QFrame#status {
    background-color: #1B1D21;
    border: 1px solid #2A2D33;
    border-radius: 8px;
}

/* The generic QLabel rule adds an 8px bottom pad for the column headers;
   inside the strip that would knock the baseline off centre. */
QFrame#status QLabel {
    background-color: transparent;
    border: none;
    padding: 0px;
}

QLabel#status_dot {
    font-size: 13pt;
    color: #9AA0A6;
    padding: 0px 1px 2px 0px;
}

/* the one word that says whether the stream is alive; the metrics beside it
   stay at body weight so the eye lands here first */
QLabel#status_state {
    font-size: 10pt;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #9AA0A6;
}

QLabel#status_detail {
    font-size: 10pt;
    color: #9AA0A6;
}

/* State colouring. These selector values are the STATE_* constants in
   gui.py; the state word is also written out in the label text, so colour
   is reinforcement and never the only signal. */
QLabel#status_dot[state="ok"],
QLabel#status_state[state="ok"] {
    color: #43B581;
}

QLabel#status_dot[state="warn"],
QLabel#status_state[state="warn"] {
    color: #E9A23C;
}

QLabel#status_dot[state="fail"],
QLabel#status_state[state="fail"] {
    color: #F87171;
}

QLabel#status_dot[state="idle"],
QLabel#status_state[state="idle"] {
    color: #9AA0A6;
}


/* --- status-strip toggles ------------------------------------------------ */
/* Keyed on the dynamic property role="toggle", not on an object name, so the
   strip's checkboxes (auto-connect, auto-recover) share one rule set and a
   third one needs no CSS at all. Qt resolves dynamic-property selectors at
   stylesheet-apply time, and StatusStrip is built before setStyleSheet(). */

QCheckBox[role="toggle"] {
    background-color: transparent;
    color: #9AA0A6;
    font-size: 10pt;
    spacing: 7px;
    padding: 0px;
    outline: none;
}

QCheckBox[role="toggle"]:hover {
    color: #E8EAED;
}

QCheckBox[role="toggle"]::indicator {
    background-color: #24262C;
    border: 1px solid #4E545F;
    border-radius: 4px;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
}

QCheckBox[role="toggle"]::indicator:hover {
    border-color: #6B76F0;
}

/* No image: the checked state is a filled accent square. An SVG tick would
   need a second asset and would not recolour with the theme. */
QCheckBox[role="toggle"]::indicator:checked {
    background-color: #5561E8;
    border-color: #5561E8;
}

QCheckBox[role="toggle"]::indicator:checked:hover {
    background-color: #5C68EE;
    border-color: #6B76F0;
}

QCheckBox[role="toggle"]:focus {
    color: #E8EAED;
}

QCheckBox[role="toggle"]:focus::indicator {
    border-color: #6B76F0;
}


/* --- tooltips ------------------------------------------------------------ */

QToolTip {
    background-color: #131417;
    border: 1px solid #383C44;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: #E8EAED;
    font-size: 10pt;
    padding: 6px 8px;
}
